{"title":"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/9580b15ecb95e817f4cc6603baaa03ed71254759.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,D,E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie, in that order, on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c65a0b904f8f63efdc2b5abfef3f4f05b2d3f990.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AF}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, dividing it into five segments, each of length 1. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is not on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9daba06f5ec9c5069f24bbeab9c7151ab4f68c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b5df2c499e5b2575bf9c1cb5d3dbabec7c54dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{GD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />, and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33bfa2720820ef9c158e3de47cbc9e3f905b622a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{GF}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />. The line segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/401cf1f2573c35d78a1ce8d7c76e1b748b7e7620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{HC}, \\overline{JE},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"69\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f0f6aa257bd96696d97454bb777b1a283069e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AG}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> are parallel. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/cce34e1167120abe069006227896d9fd72585e21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HC/JE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86cce01db8b17c5801cd663af256d40a1380f5ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 5/4 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 4/3 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 3/2 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 5/3 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"403\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First we can draw an image.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f36a37fb3fee1ec7e6c9eb3326ff0df1b01aedbe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.8 cm);  pair A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H, J;  A = (0,0); B = (1,0); C = (2,0); D = (3,0); E = (4,0); F = (5,0); G = (-1.5,4); H = extension(D, G, C, C + G - A); J = extension(F, G, E, E + G - A);  draw(A--F--G--cycle); draw(B--G); draw(C--G); draw(D--G); draw(E--G); draw(C--H); draw(E--J);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, S); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, S); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, SE); label(&quot;$G$&quot;, G, NW); label(&quot;$H$&quot;, H, W); label(&quot;$J$&quot;, J, NE); [/asy]\" width=\"292\" height=\"195\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f0f6aa257bd96696d97454bb777b1a283069e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AG}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baf06e5af8cfb43ec7280a9e284f6a338d8b6175.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CH}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> are parallel, triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/2959f4d76da21a84e4e6fdc2a8402fbd68698902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle GAD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed73c66a56a4eaa67876430ba444a7f26427227.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle HCD$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> are similar. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/c/f6c342940978de878b2c7fbe6c8cd7f2220e7978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CH}{AG} = \\frac{CD}{AD} = \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f0f6aa257bd96696d97454bb777b1a283069e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AG}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0d24b907c6febb5b90faabbd0dbaeb6041e69f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{JE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> are parallel, triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d0f4ec670f4492680408aad5326a289cd508ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle GAF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038b0468ae56e253628ea9889e0bf3f3022d1302.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle JEF$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> are similar. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fcaa3636e8ce318ce297c8fb593d94f000668b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{EJ}{AG} = \\frac{EF}{AF} = \\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/d/00da3bc67038a43770d563e3228259bb2ecf6f3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CH}{EJ} = \\left(\\frac{CH}{AG}\\right)\\div\\left(\\frac{EJ}{AG}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\div\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right) = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"374\" height=\"48\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec9a10b2b320d7be3148c6fbc51b90b21e467eef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(D) 5/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"68\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As angle F is clearly congruent to itself, we get from AA similarity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/f/43ff4c9faf5e02af8a50292dea7317faa9700c38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AGF \\sim \\triangle EJF$\" width=\"139\" height=\"13\" />; hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a1bb37af5a1396cba01fc22b20d29eaaf9f920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {AG}{JE} =5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/f/47f8959842cf85c2646c4e2b3e830bc0fea414e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {AG}{HC} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0cdf7d13c10ad5ac9e4ba87361b72b681385b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {HC}{JE}=\\left(\\frac{AG}{JE}\\right)\\left(\\frac{HC}{AG}\\right) = \\boxed{\\frac {5}{3}\\Rightarrow \\text{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"284\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume an arbitrary value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b11eccf363d2a68685340dc0b302ccba193de92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> WLOG. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f0f6aa257bd96696d97454bb777b1a283069e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AG}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baf06e5af8cfb43ec7280a9e284f6a338d8b6175.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CH}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" /> are parallel, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/2959f4d76da21a84e4e6fdc2a8402fbd68698902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle GAD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed73c66a56a4eaa67876430ba444a7f26427227.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle HCD$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" /> are similar. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b658a0fe2d2aeaf059dcfc6a839c901838e027b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AD}{CD}=3=\\frac{GA}{HC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"39\" /> which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce812d04e4d580bbd1b0f4065c0563339ebfbe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HC=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />. By the same logic, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/148abdc662d93b7952af84c94e4a99144c47433e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JE=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63a4e570418535545f1c2a83f0978f2de8d4ce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{HC}{JE}=\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AU2PJeMZ7R0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AU2PJeMZ7R0</a>    ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A\">2002 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017143113\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 299/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7618/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.189      1 -total\n 58.73%    8.333      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 40.36%    5.727      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7482:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017143113 and revision id 194125. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}